to create new directory
New-Item -Path "C:\" -Name "LabFiles" -ItemType "directory"   

to download files from github
([System.Net.WebClient]::new()).DownloadFile('https://github.com/MicrosoftLearning/PL-400_Microsoft-Power-Platform-Developer/archive/master.zip', 'C:\LabFiles\master.zip')


Expand ZIP file
Expand-Archive -Path 'C:\LabFiles\master.zip' -DestinationPath 'C:\LabFiles'

Move files to C:\LabFiles
Move-item -Path "C:\LabFiles\PL-400_Microsoft-Power-Platform-Developer-master\Allfiles\Labs\*" -Destination "C:\LabFiles" -confirm: $false


Delete files that are not needed
Remove-item 'C:\LabFiles\PL-400_Microsoft-Power-Platform-Developer-master' -recurse -force


Delete ZIP file
Remove-item 'C:\LabFiles\master.zip'



download data migration utility through command prompt

nuget Install Microsoft.CrmSdk.XrmTooling.ConfigurationMigration.Wpf -Version 9.1.0.185


Locate the newly created folder:
Local Disk (C:) -> Users -> Admin -> .nuget -> Packages -> Microsoft.CrmSdk.XrmTooling.ConfigurationMigration.Wpf -> 9.1.0.185 -> Tools
Once inside the correct folder, find DataMigrationUtility.exe and launch it from here.


launch CMT tool: Launch the Configuration Migration Tool using the following command:
pac tool cmtllie
